      "part": "worked_solution",
      "original_record": "history",
      "value": "The cardinality of a finite set $A$ is the number of elements in $A.$ \n\nLet's start by listing all the elements of $A:$\n\n$$\n1,\\,\\{10,12\\},\\,15,\\,\\{22,26,28\\},\\,\\{42,62\\}\n$$\n\nNote that $\\{10,12\\},$ $\\{22,26,28\\},$ and $\\{42,62\\}$ each count as single elements of $A.$\n\nSince $A$ has $5$ elements, the cardinality is $|A|=5.$",
